{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Defn","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Defn","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.isUnit_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.isUnit_T","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L199-L202","doc":"**Each generator is invertible** whenever `q` is, so the presentation factors through\nthe braid group and `σ_s⁻¹` in the skein dictionary (§7a) denotes an actual element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.hom_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.hom_ext","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L193-L197","doc":"Two algebra maps agreeing on the simple reflections are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.universal_property","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.universal_property","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L181-L191","doc":"**The universal property of the Iwahori–Hecke algebra.**\n\nPreviously: existence proved by hand, uniqueness recorded as `axiom universal_property`\non the ground that the container had no `lake` binary.  Both are now discharged by\n`QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.exists_unique_lift`, and the target may be any `R`-algebra\nrather than a commutative one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.IsHeckeAlgebraMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.IsHeckeAlgebraMap","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L168-L179","doc":"**Hecke algebra map**: a family on the simple reflections satisfying *both* defining\nfamilies.\n\nThe old predicate of this name asserted only the quadratic relation, and asserted it for\nevery `s : W`.  Its docstring defended the over-quantification by saying the restriction\nto simple reflections \"happens upstream ... the caller passes an `f` that is only\nnontrivial on `S`\" — a constraint on callers, not on the predicate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.T_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.T_braid","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L157-L161","doc":"**The braid relation holds** — the half the old construction was missing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.T_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.T_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L152-L155","doc":"**The quadratic relation holds.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.T","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L142-L148","doc":"The generator `T_s`, for `s` a **simple reflection**.\n\nNote the index: `s : S`, not `s : W`.  That is the substance of the rebuild — the old\n`T` accepted any group element and asserted a quadratic relation for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.instAlgebra_iwahoriHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.instAlgebra_iwahoriHecke","kind":"instance","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L137-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.instRing_iwahoriHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.instRing_iwahoriHecke","kind":"instance","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L132-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.IwahoriHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.IwahoriHecke","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L126-L130","doc":"**The Iwahori–Hecke algebra** of `(W, S)` over `R` at parameter `q`, in the Iwahori\nnormalisation `(T_s − q)(T_s + 1) = 0` together with the braid relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.coxeterMatrixOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.coxeterMatrixOn","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Defn.lean#L118-L124","doc":"The Coxeter matrix carried by a subset of a group: `m(s,t) = orderOf (s · t)`.\n\nFor a genuine Coxeter system this is the Coxeter matrix on the nose.  Nothing downstream\nrequires that `S` be one — the construction is well-defined for any subset, and a caller\nthat has a `CoxeterSystem` may pass its matrix instead. ","signatureChunk":0}]}